Performance review. The code or data is supplied inline. This is a diagnosis-only task: do NOT edit or create any file and do not run commands; respond with findings and a proposed fix as text. Be explicit about what you measured versus what you are inferring.

This function backs `yakos cost --by agent` and is called once with ~5,000 agents' worth of dispatch-log lines (the log is ~40 MB NDJSON).

```go
func costForAgents(agents []string, logPath string) (map[string]float64, error) {
	out := make(map[string]float64, len(agents))
	for _, a := range agents {
		data, err := os.ReadFile(logPath)
		if err != nil {
			return nil, err
		}
		for _, line := range strings.Split(string(data), "\n") {
			var rec struct {
				Agent string  `json:"agent"`
				Cost  float64 `json:"cost_usd"`
			}
			if json.Unmarshal([]byte(line), &rec) == nil && rec.Agent == a {
				out[a] += rec.Cost
			}
		}
	}
	return out, nil
}
```
Identify the dominant cost, state its complexity, and give the fixed version.
